17. INTERVIEW-READY SUMMARY
============================================================

Tool orchestration controls how multiple tools execute and
exchange data.

Sequential orchestration:
Used when one tool depends on another.

Parallel orchestration:
Used when operations are independent and can run simultaneously.

Conditional orchestration:
Used when execution needs deterministic routing based on
status, validation, or data quality.

For production resilience, combine them with:

• Data contracts
• Data transformations
• Aggregation
• Timeouts
• Retry with exponential backoff
• Partial failure handling
• Cache fallback
• Circuit breakers
• Explicit fallback paths
• Data-quality validation


